---
const props = [
  {
    id: "P1 — confidentiality",
    title: "Plaintext stays encrypted.",
    body: `Input <code>x</code> and output <code>y</code> are not revealed to any network adversary or to an honest-but-curious Operator. Holds against passive and active wire attackers under TFHE security.`,
  },
  {
    id: "P2 — accountability",
    title: "The Operator cannot deny what it signed.",
    body: `A valid Receipt cryptographically attributes the claimed <code>(function, input_hash, output_hash, policy)</code> tuple to the Operator's <code>pk_op</code>. Cryptographic prevention (ZK proofs) is targeted in Phase 4.`,
  },
  {
    id: "P3 — non-repudiation",
    title: "Signatures are forever.",
    body: `No party — including the Operator — can credibly deny having produced the signature, absent compromise of <code>sk_op</code>. Verifiers acquire <code>pk_op</code> through a trusted out-of-band channel.`,
  },
  {
    id: "P4 — replay resistance",
    title: "Each request is one-shot.",
    body: `A Receipt cannot be reused for a different <code>ComputeRequest</code>; a request cannot be replayed within the Operator's acceptance window. Enforced by 16-byte CSPRNG nonces and timestamp mirroring.`,
  },
  {
    id: "P5 — portability",
    title: "Verify offline. Anywhere. Forever.",
    body: `Given only <code>(Receipt, pk_op)</code>, any Verifier can validate without contacting the Operator, at any time after issuance. A regulator in 2030 verifies a Receipt issued in 2026.`,
  },
  {
    id: "P6 — backend-agnosticism",
    title: "Same envelope, any primitive.",
    body: `Signing and validation logic do not change when the backend changes. Future TEE, MPC, and ZK backends inherit P1–P5 by construction via localized extensions to the wire format.`,
  },
];
---

<section id="properties">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-num"><span>§ 05 — Security Properties</span></div>
    <h2>What the protocol <em>actually</em> proves.</h2>

    <p style="max-width: 60ch;">
      v0.1 makes a deliberate split: <em>cryptographic prevention</em> for plaintext
      confidentiality, <em>cryptographic accountability</em> for computation integrity.
      Honest specs distinguish what they prove from what they make attributable.
    </p>

    <figure
      class="figure"
      data-label="Fig. 04 — The dual guarantee"
      style="margin-top: 48px;"
    >
      <svg
        viewBox="0 0 1100 320"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
        role="img"
        aria-labelledby="dualTitle"
      >
        <title id="dualTitle"
          >Two halves of the v0.1 guarantee: prevention vs. accountability.</title
        >
        <defs>
          <pattern
            id="confHatch"
            patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
            width="6"
            height="6"
            patternTransform="rotate(45)"
          >
            <line
              x1="0"
              y1="0"
              x2="0"
              y2="6"
              stroke="#b8341c"
              stroke-width="0.7"
              opacity="0.45"></line>
          </pattern>
          <pattern
            id="accHatch"
            patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"
            width="6"
            height="6"
            patternTransform="rotate(-45)"
          >
            <line
              x1="0"
              y1="0"
              x2="0"
              y2="6"
              stroke="#8a6c2c"
              stroke-width="0.7"
              opacity="0.55"></line>
          </pattern>
        </defs>

        <g>
          <rect
            x="20"
            y="20"
            width="510"
            height="280"
            fill="url(#confHatch)"
            stroke="#b8341c"
            stroke-width="1.2"></rect>
          <rect x="20" y="20" width="510" height="36" fill="#b8341c"></rect>
          <text
            x="40"
            y="44"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="11"
            fill="#f4f1ea"
            letter-spacing="2">P1 · CONFIDENTIALITY</text>
          <text
            x="510"
            y="44"
            text-anchor="end"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="11"
            fill="#f4f1ea"
            letter-spacing="2">CRYPTOGRAPHIC PREVENTION</text>

          <text
            x="40"
            y="100"
            font-family="Newsreader, serif"
            font-style="italic"
            font-size="32"
            fill="#14110d">The Operator</text>
          <text
            x="40"
            y="138"
            font-family="Newsreader, serif"
            font-style="italic"
            font-size="32"
            fill="#14110d">cannot see x.</text>

          <text
            x="40"
            y="186"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="12"
            fill="#2a251d">guarantee:  TFHE encryption of inputs</text>
          <text
            x="40"
            y="206"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="12"
            fill="#2a251d">defense:    cryptanalytic intractability</text>
          <text
            x="40"
            y="226"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="12"
            fill="#2a251d">recourse:   none required — broken means</text>
          <text
            x="40"
            y="244"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="12"
            fill="#2a251d">{`            128-bit security is broken`}</text>

          <text
            x="40"
            y="280"
            font-family="Newsreader, serif"
            font-size="14"
            font-style="italic"
            fill="#b8341c">→ mathematical, not legal</text>
        </g>

        <g>
          <line
            x1="565"
            y1="20"
            x2="565"
            y2="300"
            stroke="#1a1712"
            stroke-width="1"
            stroke-dasharray="3 4"></line>
          <circle
            cx="565"
            cy="160"
            r="20"
            fill="#f4f1ea"
            stroke="#1a1712"
            stroke-width="1.2"></circle>
          <text
            x="565"
            y="160"
            text-anchor="middle"
            dominant-baseline="central"
            font-family="Newsreader, serif"
            font-style="italic"
            font-size="16"
            fill="#14110d">vs</text>
        </g>

        <g>
          <rect
            x="600"
            y="20"
            width="480"
            height="280"
            fill="url(#accHatch)"
            stroke="#8a6c2c"
            stroke-width="1.2"></rect>
          <rect x="600" y="20" width="480" height="36" fill="#8a6c2c"></rect>
          <text
            x="620"
            y="44"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="11"
            fill="#f4f1ea"
            letter-spacing="2">P2 · INTEGRITY</text>
          <text
            x="1060"
            y="44"
            text-anchor="end"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="11"
            fill="#f4f1ea"
            letter-spacing="2">ACCOUNTABILITY (V0.1)</text>

          <text
            x="620"
            y="100"
            font-family="Newsreader, serif"
            font-style="italic"
            font-size="32"
            fill="#14110d">The Operator</text>
          <text
            x="620"
            y="138"
            font-family="Newsreader, serif"
            font-style="italic"
            font-size="32"
            fill="#14110d">cannot deny.</text>

          <text
            x="620"
            y="186"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="12"
            fill="#2a251d">guarantee:  Ed25519 signature over JCS</text>
          <text
            x="620"
            y="206"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="12"
            fill="#2a251d">defense:    non-repudiable attestation</text>
          <text
            x="620"
            y="226"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="12"
            fill="#2a251d">recourse:   legal, contractual, reputational</text>
          <text
            x="620"
            y="244"
            font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace"
            font-size="12"
            fill="#2a251d">{`            — ZK prevention in Phase 4`}</text>

          <text
            x="620"
            y="280"
            font-family="Newsreader, serif"
            font-size="14"
            font-style="italic"
            fill="#8a6c2c">→ attribution, not prevention (today)</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <div class="figure-caption">
        Fig. 04 — <strong
          >An honest spec distinguishes what it proves from what it merely makes
          attributable.</strong
        >
      </div>
    </figure>

    <div class="props">
      {
        props.map((p) => (
          <div class="prop">
            <div class="prop-id">{p.id}</div>
            <h3>{p.title}</h3>
            <p set:html={p.body} />
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
